# Neuromorphic Audio Wake-Word Detection — CNL Spec
# Demo 4: A small SNN detects a wake word using spike-encoded audio features.
# Uses temporal coincidence detection with axonal delays (cochlear-inspired).

The network MUST operate WITH timestep of 1 ms

The network MUST contain an excitatory sensory population of 1 neurons
The network MUST contain an excitatory interneuron population of 45 neurons
The network MUST contain an excitatory motor population of 1 neurons

# Sensory population fires on audio onset features
The sensory population MUST fire ONLY IF membrane potential exceeds 0.6

# Interneuron integrates onset timing before final detection
The interneuron population MUST fire ONLY IF membrane potential exceeds 0.7

# Motor population fires when temporal coincidence is detected
The motor population MUST emit a spike ONLY IF membrane potential exceeds 0.9

# Refractory periods matched to audio feature timescales
The sensory population MUST NOT fire DURING the refractory period of 0.001 seconds
The motor population MUST NOT fire DURING the refractory period of 0.005 seconds

# Time constants: fast for onset detection, slower for integration
The sensory population membrane potential MUST decay WITH time constant of 0.005 seconds
The motor population membrane potential MUST decay WITH time constant of 0.02 seconds

The sensory population MUST project to interneuron population
The interneuron population MUST project to motor population
The sensory population MUST project to motor population

The connection from sensory population to interneuron population MUST have WITH synaptic weight of 1.0
The connection from interneuron population to motor population MUST have WITH synaptic weight of 1.6
The connection from sensory population to motor population MUST have WITH synaptic weight of 0.4

# Axonal delays for temporal coincidence detection (polychronization)
A synapse MUST have a transmission delay of 5ms

# STDP for learning temporal patterns
The connection from sensory population to interneuron population MUST strengthen IF pre fires before post WITHIN 15 ms
A synapse MUST NOT have weights exceeding 2.5
